WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:03.399
Ace was CRIMINALLY nerfed by the author of
One Piece.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:04.399
That’s right.

00:00:04.399 --> 00:00:05.790
I said it.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:11.700
Honestly, looking at what we know about Ace,
he had the potential to become one of the

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.429
strongest characters in the entire story.

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:20.269
However, because Luffys is the main character,
Ace not only never got to show his true power

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:25.760
even once, but he even had his life BRUTALLY
cut short.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:32.160
However, let’s pretend THIS never happened
[Donut Ace] and instead figure out what would

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.600
happen if Ace reached his full potential.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.050
Because picture this.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.170
Seventeen year old Ace becomes a pirate.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:44.360
He gets his fire devil fruit and starts to
make a real name for himself in the pirate

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.360
world.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.300
He LITERALLY travels the ENTIRE Grand Line,
going from places like Fishman Island all

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.039
the way to Wano where he rescued children
from Kaido’s castle.

00:00:54.039 --> 00:01:00.219
Seriously, this man is the DEFINITION of THAT
GUY.

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:07.130
And before he even turned twenty he defeated
a Warlord and fought another one for five

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.130
whole days.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:14.960
But then what happens next DESTROYED Ace’s
chance of becoming pirate king.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:20.090
Because then Whitebeard showed up [ch 552],
beat down Ace, and basically forced the fiery

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.140
young pirate onto his crew.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.830
Now, without a doubt, this worked out well
for Ace.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:31.680
He found the family he had always wanted and
was happy all the up until his death at Marineford.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:32.680
BUT…

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:39.280
And this is a big BUT, Ace joining Whitebeard’s
crew was the DEATH of his chances at growing

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.110
stronger because at this point he didn’t
really have to struggle on his own anymore.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:51.719
So yeah, being with Whitebeard definitely
killed Ace’s true potential.

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:56.860
That’s all in the past though, because let’s
imagine that Ace’s story went in a completely

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.229
new direction.

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:06.079
Originally, Ace fought the Warlord Jinbe for
five days before Whitebeard showed up, so

00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:12.530
instead of that let’s imagine that Ace defeats
Jinbe sooner and then he and his crew sailed

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.410
away before the Yonko arrived to wipe them
all out.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.730
Or if this is too unreasonable for you, maybe
Whitebeard does show up and beat down Ace,

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:26.930
but instead of inviting him on the crew maybe
Whitebeard recognizes Ace’s potential and

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.220
lets him go.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:34.209
And if this happened then Ace would be FURIOUS
that he couldn’t defeat Whitebeard, which

00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:37.590
means he is going to want to get even stronger.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:43.920
Maybe he’ll just continue to train on his
own or even seek out someone to help him reach

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.019
the next level.

00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:46.630
Either way, here’s the deal.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:51.700
Ace is now around twenty years old, and let’s
say after some more time on his own he’s

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:58.280
learned basic armament and observation haki,
since that was never confirmed in the story.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.700
So Ace is already stronger than he was originally.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:09.680
So now you might be asking, what is Ace’s
goal since he isn’t part of Whitebeard’s

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.680
crew anymore?

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:18.930
Well, the answer is simple, because if you
read the Ace novels then you should know that

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:24.150
his main goal after entering the Grand Line
was to defeat the Yonko.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:29.040
He even burned down Whitebeard’s flag in
fishman island when the Spade Pirates passed

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.590
through on their way to the new world.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:37.650
So everything that Ace does at this point
will be to grow stronger so that he can defeat

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.650
the Yonko.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.750
Before we go any further though, let’s recap
where we are timeline wise.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:48.300
At this point, Ace has been a pirate for around
three years, which is the same time that Luffy

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.010
starts his own adventure.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:55.670
However, there are some serious changes to
this story since Ace didn't join Whitebeard.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:01.129
Basically, the whole Marineford Saga is cut
out of the story because that entire plot

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:07.299
line started when Ace hunted down Blackbeard
because he betrayed Whitebeard's crew by backstabbing

00:04:07.299 --> 00:04:08.640
this guy [ch 440, Thatch].

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:14.950
This time around, Ace just doesn't care though,
so there's no getting captured by Blackbeard.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:22.350
Although, Blackbeard might go after Luffy
even more than he already did, but Luffy already

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:26.410
escaped from Blackbeard the first time [ch
236] so I’m not going to assume that the

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.750
wanna be Emperor would catch Luffy in the
first place.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:34.419
Plus, Whitebeard wouldn’t come to Marineford
to save Luffy anyway, so there wouldn’t

00:04:34.419 --> 00:04:39.100
be a giant battle unless Shanks or Luffy’s
father came to save him.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.340
But we’re getting way too off track here.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.770
This video is about Ace, not Luffy.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:49.150
But what all this means is that Whitebeard
will still be alive.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.500
However, that won’t last for long.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:55.850
Because let’s assume that after the years
of extra training, Ace finally feels like

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.680
he is ready to take on Whitebeard.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.630
So the Spade pirates roll up and challenge
the Emperor.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:09.120
And while Ace’s crewmates might get completely
wiped out, I do think Ace would be strong

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.410
enough at this point to take out Whitebeard.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:18.220
Because remember, Whitebeard is still sick,
and the longer he is in the story, the worse

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.150
he is going to get.

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:26.570
He’s still incredibly powerful though, and
it would be a legendary fight with Whitebeard’s

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:30.300
Tremor powers against Ace’s supercharged
fire blasts.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:36.270
And during the fight, I can easily see Whitebeard
being reminded of Roger while fighting Ace

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.810
which might lead to Ace revealing that he
is actually Roger’s son.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.710
And can you imagine that?

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:48.770
That single fact would just completely blow
Whitebeard’s mind AND it is going to change

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:51.150
the rest of Ace’s story forever.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.880
Because let’s just imagine that after an
exhausting battle, Ace finally defeats the

00:05:55.880 --> 00:06:00.650
sick Whitebeard, but because of the respect
they gained for each other, Ace spares Whitebeard’s

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.650
life.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.560
However, this is where things turn dark.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:11.650
Because just like at Marineford, I can imagine
Blackbeard swooping in and finishing off Whitebeard

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.120
to steal his devil fruit.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:18.030
And since the Emperor and Ace just had their
big, exhausting battle, it makes a lot of

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:21.820
sense to me that Whitebeard and his crew wouldn’t
be able to fight them off.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:26.849
So yeah, I do see Blackbeard once again killing
Whitebeard and taking his devil fruit.

00:06:26.849 --> 00:06:28.210
Shocking, right?

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:33.530
However, one important thing to add is that
I think with his dying breath, Whitebeard

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:39.430
might try to inspire Ace to find the One Piece
just like he originally did when he gave his

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:43.000
famous “The One Piece is real” line during
Marineford [ch 576].

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:49.370
He might even tell Ace the importance of what
Roger discovered or that Ace needs to find

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:50.370
the One Piece.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:55.850
So while Ace might not really know exactly
what Whitebeard is talking about, I honestly

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:59.930
think this would have a major impact on the
young pirate.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:07.400
And while he might not want to follow in his
father’s footsteps, I could see Ace ultimately

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:12.520
deciding to inherit Whitebeard’s dying will.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:23.330
Which is just incredibly ironic because Whitebeard
originally wanted Ace to be pirate king, but

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.729
the Emperor held Ace back by making him join
his crew.

00:07:26.729 --> 00:07:35.270
But now that Ace is on his own, he could very
well be inspired to do exactly what Whitebeard

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.740
wanted him to do in the first place.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:42.750
So yeah, Ace has a new goal and a new sworn
enemy in Blackbeard.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:47.759
But with Whitebeard out of the picture, we
have to consider who would fill the void in

00:07:47.759 --> 00:07:49.370
the Emperor Ranks.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:55.970
It could be Blackbeard just like normal or
it could also be Ace, since he defeated Whitebeard

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.150
in the first place.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:02.290
For now, let’s go with Ace being considered
an Emperor of the Sea, because come on, it

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:06.520
is just so incredibly cool to have Yonko Ace.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:11.289
Now of course, the first part of Ace’s new
mission to become pirate king is to reach

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:16.650
Laugh Tale, but the surprising thing you have
to remember is that very few people in the

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:22.930
one piece world actually know how to even
find the directions to the legendary island.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:27.020
So to start Ace would need to do one of two
things.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:31.770
First, someone could tell him about the poneglyphs
and how you have to collect all four Road

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:32.959
Poneglyphs to reach Laugh Tale.

00:08:32.959 --> 00:08:37.959
And this could be someone like Marco, who
has been with Whitebeard long enough to most

00:08:37.959 --> 00:08:39.519
likely know about the Poneglyphs.

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:44.440
Honestly, though, that shortcut route feels
a bit cheap so let's go with the true way

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:50.400
which is that someone is supposed to find
the final island of the Grand Line, Loadstar

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.630
island.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:57.671
This is the island where Roger and his crew
originally learned about the poneglyphs, so

00:08:57.671 --> 00:09:04.120
let’s set Ace on that same path and say
that the Spade pirates sail past all of the

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:07.480
other Yonko’s territory and reach Lodestar.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:14.110
This is where we have to start guessing though
because we don’t actually know what is on

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.110
Lodestar island.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:19.300
It could be a poneglyph which explains all
about the other poneglyphs, including the

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.600
Road Poneglyphs which lead to Laugh Tale.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:27.410
Or it could be some sort of ancient civilization
still living on Loadstar who helps guide people

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:29.920
to find the poneglyphs.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:36.190
But whatever the case, there is one major
problem for Ace and the Spade pirates.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:42.300
Which is that even if Ace finds the Poneglyphs,
he doesn’t have anyone who can actually

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.800
read them.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:49.760
So to solve this, let’s just imagine that
Ace inherited his father’s Voice of All

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:57.670
Things ability, which lets Ace somewhat understand
what the poneglyphs say.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:02.770
And although this doesn’t solve the problem
for good, this is enough for them to start

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:06.970
their journey collecting poneglyphs back at
the start of the Grand Line.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:13.250
This leads to my personal favorite part of
this scenario which is when Ace reunites with

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.360
Luffy.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:16.820
And oh, boy this is going to be fun.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:21.330
And while they probably wouldn’t meet at
Alabasta since the timing is way different

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:25.831
here, Ace would still likely visit many of
the same places that Luffy did early on in

00:10:25.831 --> 00:10:26.831
his journey.

00:10:26.831 --> 00:10:30.880
For example, there was a poneglyph in Alabasta
and another on Fishman island.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.800
So eventually, I would imagine that they meet
up, just like they did in the original story

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:36.800
[ch 157].

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.950
What’s really interesting though is that
when these two originally met they had this

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.030
interesting conversation about becoming pirate
king.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:49.570
Obviously, that is Luffy’s goal, but now
Ace himself is on that same path and he has

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:52.080
a WAY BIGGER head start.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:57.800
So even though these two friends are now technically
rivals, I just think that Luffy is nowhere

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:03.600
near strong enough yet to be a serious threat
to Ace, so Ace would likely just move on with

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:04.649
his journey.

00:11:04.649 --> 00:11:10.100
Although, there is one HUGE CONFLICT that
will need to be addressed at some point.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:15.690
Because even though Ace has the Voice of All
Things, that really isn’t enough to truly

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.960
interpret the Road Poneglyphs and reach Laugh
Tale.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:25.900
Even Roger needed someone who could actually
read them in order to find the legendary island

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:26.900
[ch 966 Roger talking with Oden, Whitebeard].

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:30.810
And with Nico Robin being the only person
we know at this point in the story who could

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:35.300
read the poneglyphs, Ace would surely want
her to be on his crew.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:41.940
So there’s a chance he could try to take
her OR that Robin herself might want to go

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.940
with Ace.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:46.480
But for now let’s assume Ace doesn’t know
about Robin’s ability to read the Poneglyphs,

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:53.010
or that Robin is already invested in the Straw
Hats, so Ace simply moves on.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.010
For now…

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:58.730
Now, Ace is well on his way to becoming pirate
king, but this journey is going to lead him

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.779
back to the New World.

00:12:00.779 --> 00:12:05.690
And let’s assume this takes a long time,
at least a year or two as the Spade Pirates

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:06.690
continue their journey.

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:10.600
It’s not like there’s a map or anything
that shows where all the important poneglyphs

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.600
are.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.600
Unless…

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:13.600
Wait, maybe there is.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:17.060
Which would be completely awesome, but we
don’t know for sure.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:22.050
Also keep in mind we are missing some major
world events here, like no marineford as we

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:27.240
said earlier, which also means no normal timeskip
for the straw hat crew, although I would imagine

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:31.459
Luffy and his crew would need some kind of
training arc in order to survive in the New

00:12:31.459 --> 00:12:32.459
World.

00:12:32.459 --> 00:12:37.610
But all this means that as Ace is collecting
the poneglyphs and searching for Laugh Tale,

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:45.050
he would 100% need to eventually fight Big
Mom and Kaido since they possessed two of

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:46.180
the Road Poneglyphs.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:51.420
And before that let’s assume that Ace somehow
found his way to Zou and was able to get a

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:53.389
copy of the Road Poneglyph there.

00:12:53.389 --> 00:12:57.680
I mean, I’m not really sure how that would
happen since the Spade pirates don’t have

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:01.889
a mink on their crew, but who knows maybe
they get a new crewmate along the way who

00:13:01.889 --> 00:13:02.889
is a mink.

00:13:02.889 --> 00:13:07.630
Or maybe they use their connections with their
friends on Wano to find someone who can take

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:08.630
them there.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:13.769
But with that one out of the way, we now have
to face Big Mom and Kaido.

00:13:13.769 --> 00:13:18.589
Certainly, the Spade pirates themselves are
not all that powerful, which would mean Ace

00:13:18.589 --> 00:13:23.260
would need to basically be strong enough to
take on the entire Yonko crew.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:26.340
Which I don’t know if Ace is THAT strong.

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:31.430
Which means it makes perfect sense for Ace
to team up with another pirate who has the

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:32.430
same goal.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.389
Oh, I don’t know, maybe someone like Luffy!

00:13:35.389 --> 00:13:40.139
That’s right because by this time the Straw
Hat pirates have entered the New World.

00:13:40.139 --> 00:13:44.680
And you might think it is cheating for them
to team up, but we already know Luffy teamed

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:49.320
up with a lot of pirates to take down Kaido,
so I think it’s fair for Luffy and Ace to

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.760
work together to defeat the current Emperors.&nbsp;

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:57.200
Plus, Ace already has ties to Wano from his
time there early in his pirate career, so

00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:02.040
let’s just say that instead of Luffy teaming
up with Kid and Law, Ace joins the party to

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.660
take down the Yonko.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:08.639
This could happen separately on Whole Cake
Island and then Wano, or the Emperors could

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:11.529
team up like they did during the Wano arc.

00:14:11.529 --> 00:14:15.860
And I don’t think it really matters who
fights who at this point, but the important

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:21.250
thing is that with their combined forces and
the people of Wano, Luffy and Ace should be

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:25.430
strong enough to take down Kaido and Big Mom.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.550
The major, unavoidable problem is coming up
next though.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:33.209
Because at this point both Ace and Luffy have
three Road Poneglyphs.

00:14:33.209 --> 00:14:37.910
Ace is a legitimate Yonko and Luffy has just
awakened Gear 5.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:42.670
However, Luffy has one major advantage over
Ace.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:43.670
Nico Robin.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:47.570
Because certainly at this point Ace would
realize that the Voice of All Things simply

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:50.470
isn’t enough to figure out how to get to
Laugh Tale.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:55.120
He probably needs to know exactly what the
Road Poneglyphs say, so he desperately needs

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.779
someone on his crew who can read them.

00:14:57.779 --> 00:15:02.850
Now there is this guy [Sukiyaki ch 1053],
but I doubt he wants to leave Wano, so that

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:05.680
just leaves one person who can read them.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:10.529
Now, of course I doubt Robin would want to
go with Ace, but if Ace truly is determined

00:15:10.529 --> 00:15:14.750
to become pirate king, then he will stop at
nothing to fulfill his goals.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:19.040
Which ultimately means that these two crews
will need to fight.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:20.690
Yeah, shocking right?

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:25.880
But that’s what it takes to become pirate
king.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:31.810
And I can just imagine Luffy and Ace going
all out against each other.

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:35.459
Ace’s flames would be extremely powerful
by this point.

00:15:35.459 --> 00:15:41.579
He is basically like a full on fiery god,
but Luffy also has his Gear 5 powers, which

00:15:41.579 --> 00:15:45.750
as we’ve seen can let him take out even
the strongest of characters.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:49.330
So I really don’t know how this battle would
go.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:54.399
But in the end, I seriously doubt they would
go all the way to killing each other.

00:15:54.399 --> 00:16:01.500
In fact, they might even decide to end this
fight in one of the most controversial ways

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:02.500
possible.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:03.500
Let me explain.

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:08.069
If you go back to the arc just after Skypeia,
we were introduced to the concept of a Davy

00:16:08.069 --> 00:16:09.069
Back Fight.

00:16:09.069 --> 00:16:13.709
Now this is a real pirate competition in the
One Piece world where pirate crews can challenge

00:16:13.709 --> 00:16:16.949
each other in order to steal members from
each other’s crews.

00:16:16.949 --> 00:16:24.460
And as silly as this arc was, it really seems
like pirates take this seriously, and there

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:30.500
is even speculation that the legendary pirate
Rocks D. Xebec used Davy Back fights to gather

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:32.050
his impressive crew.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:37.330
So anyway, you might be wondering, “what
exactly is a Davy back fight”?

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:44.990
Well, we’ve only seen one in the main story,
but it involved a three stage competition.

00:16:44.990 --> 00:16:46.980
First a boat race around an island [ch 307].

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:50.930
A game called Groggy Ring [ch 309], which
is kinda like soccer except that one player

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.889
on each team is the ball.

00:16:52.889 --> 00:16:57.649
And finally a one on one duel where the person
who gets knocked out of the ring first loses

00:16:57.649 --> 00:16:58.649
[ch 313-314].

00:16:58.649 --> 00:17:02.459
And of course, the winner of these events
gets to take members from the other person’s

00:17:02.459 --> 00:17:03.459
crew.

00:17:03.459 --> 00:17:07.750
Now, we aren’t sure if this is how every
single davy back fight works since we’ve

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.559
only seen one in the entire story, but for
the sake of this video, let’s assume that

00:17:11.559 --> 00:17:18.089
Ace and the Spade pirates win this event,
and Nico Robin is forced to join Ace’s crew.

00:17:18.089 --> 00:17:23.120
We could even say that the entire Straw Hats
are forced to join the Spade pirates, but

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:29.390
I’m not actually sure if Luffy would ever
work under someone else, so for now let’s

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:32.900
just assume that Robin is the one that joins
the Spade Pirates.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:37.160
So that means that Ace now has a clear path
toward becoming pirate king.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:41.771
All he has to do is find the fourth Road poneglyph,
which is likely being protected by the Emperor

00:17:41.771 --> 00:17:45.830
Shanks and the giants in Elbaf, and then make
his way to Laugh Tale.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:49.263
And while that is no easy task, we do know
that Ace already knows Shanks [ch 552], so

00:17:49.263 --> 00:17:53.710
while I don’t think that Shanks would just
give Ace the Road Poneglpyh, if we can imagine

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:57.929
that Luffy would somehow obtain it from Elbaf
then the same applies to Ace.

00:17:57.929 --> 00:18:04.050
There is just one other major problem though
because in all this time we still have the

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:09.500
MASSIVE threat of Blackbeard who will likely
be Ace’s final challenge before becoming

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.500
pirate king.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:15.190
But with all that’s gone on in the story,
plus Ace’s extra motivation to take down

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:22.740
the person who killed Whitebeard, I just have
to imagine that Ace would come out on top.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:28.250
Which just shows how much potential Fire-Fist
Ace truly had.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:34.700
Actually though, this brings me to another
character with INSANE untapped potential.

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:38.450
Because if you’ve ever thought that it is
SO CRIMINALLY UNFAIR that Luffy and Zoro get

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.210
all the attention from the Straw Hats, you
are not alone.

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:46.900
Because Sanji is just as deserving as the
other two, so to hype him up even more, I

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:52.500
figured out the perfect devil fruit to make
Sanji into a god-tier fighter.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.299
And you can watch that video right here.

00:18:54.299 --> 00:18:57.370
Shanks for watching and I’ll see you in
the next one.

